# erlinit.config for Xiaomi Pad 6S Pro (sheng)
#
# erlinit auto-detects the OTP release under /srv/erlang (see
# https://github.com/nerves-project/erlinit#release-setup) and prefers the
# ERTS bundled inside the release itself, matching this project's
# `include_erts: &Nerves.Release.erts/0` release config - no --release-path
# or --boot needed.
#
# Rebooting (not hanging) on Erlang VM exit/fatal error is already erlinit's
# default behavior, so not spelled out explicitly here.
#
# --hostname-pattern with no %s placeholder: erlinit's hostname_sprintf only
# treats `%` specially, so a plain literal string is copied through as-is -
# no --uniqueid-exec/boardid package needed since there's only one of this
# device. Without this, the OS hostname was Buildroot's static default
# "buildroot" (confirmed via `hostname` at the IEx prompt), and while
# mdns_lite's separate static "nerves" alias (see config/target.exs) does
# make `nerves.local` resolve, `mix nerves.discover` also filters on the
# hostname/service-name actually starting with "nerves"/"nerves-"
# (deps/nerves_discovery's filter_nerves/1) - "buildroot" fails that check
# even though the device is otherwise fully reachable and SSH-able.
-n nerves-sheng

# Boot signals (before Erlang VM starts)
#
# LED blink: 10 rapid blinks + 1 second hold = erlinit is running, userspace alive
#   If you see LED blinks, the kernel booted and erlinit started successfully.
#   No LED blinks = stuck in kernel or bootloader, never reached userspace.
#
# Audio beep: 3 beeps @ 1000Hz = audio subsystem working
#   If LED blinks but no beeps, audio failed (driver/firmware issue).
#   If both: device is alive and working, waiting for Erlang to start.

-c /usr/bin/boot-led-blink.sh

# Loads ath12k (WiFi) and the audio driver chain - see that script's header
# comment for why this is needed at all (no udev/mdev on Nerves to
# auto-load them, unlike the debian-sheng reference this kernel config is
# otherwise matched against). Must run before boot-beep.sh, which needs
# audio actually loaded to do anything.
-c /usr/bin/load-hw-modules.sh

-c /usr/bin/boot-beep.sh

# TEMPORARY debug aid: stop erlinit's default reboot-on-exit/reboot-on-fatal
# behavior so a failed/crashing Erlang VM leaves the board sitting at a
# reachable state (usb0/VintageNetDirect + sshd, if it got that far) instead
# of silently rebooting with zero trace. Remove once boot is confirmed
# stable - see nerves-project/erlinit README "Rebooting or hanging when the
# Erlang VM exits".
--hang-on-exit
--hang-on-fatal